hexagon: give init_fastdiv_values no divisor of zero in the matmul params
Fold-into: upstream/hexagon-host

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus every patch of the series before this one.

Finding mm-id-div-zero of fuzz-hexhost, task #156. The matmul params of the
host (ggml_hexagon_precompute_matmul_params_impl, which supports_op also
calls) give five divisors to init_fastdiv_values, and init_fastdiv_values
divides by its argument. For MUL_MAT_ID, ne02 is the expert count and ne12
the token count. Thus one token with more than one expert gives
ne12 / ne02 = 0, and an empty src1 gives ne11 = 0. The division by zero is
undefined behavior. On x86 it stops the process with SIGFPE. On arm64 the
division gives 0, thus the phone did not stop.

This patch gives init_fastdiv_values the divisor 1 in place of 0.
init_fastdiv_values(1) gives the values that the arm64 division by 0 gave,
thus the DSP gets the same kernel params on the phone.
ggml_hexagon_precompute_fused_mmnx_params has the same five lines. It runs
only in the fusion of an op batch, the host puts no empty op into a batch,
and for a dense product ggml_can_mul_mat gives ne12 / ne02 >= 1.

This patch removes the entry "integer-divide-by-zero:^init_fastdiv_values("
of tests/sanitizers/ubsan.supp and the recovery of integer-divide-by-zero of
tests/sanitizers/ubsan.cmake (rule L8).

Evidence (2026-09-23):
- The regression input tests/fuzz/hexhost/regress/kparams/mm-id-div-zero.bin
  stops with SIGFPE in init_fastdiv_values (hex-fastdiv.h:22), called from
  the supports_op of MUL_MAT_ID, before this patch. With the five patches of
  fuzz-hexhost it gives no finding in the asan build, debug and release.
- The kparams fuzzer with this condition on ran 6 times for 100 s with the
  patches: no finding.
- The phone check of the five patches of fuzz-hexhost together (OnePlus 13,
  the 2B Q8_0 on HTP0, thermal status 0, cpu7 cap 4.32 GHz, battery 27.6 to
  27.7 °C, MemAvailable 8.9 to 9.5 GB):
  - test-backend-ops on HTP0, the MUL_MAT_ID cases (390 cases): pass before
    and after. The four other op groups also pass before and after.
  - llama-bench tg32 -r 3 after one warmup at 23.76 t/s: before 23.56 ±
    0.10, after 23.59 ± 0.27, before 23.63 ± 0.13, after 23.57 ± 0.11 t/s.
  - llama-speculative-simple with the MTP draft of depth 4, temperature 0,
    64 tokens: before 23.589 and 23.685 t/s, after 24.076 and 24.029 t/s.
    Each run accepts 44 drafts (52.381 %), and the four runs give the same
    text.

Measurement: the patch adds one compare for each of five values of the
matmul params. The host instructions for each decode token of the 4B Q8_0
graph (x86, the real-graph tool with the fake DSP, perf stat) are in the
headers of fuzz-hexhost/0001 to 0003. The tg32 of the phone check does not
change.

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/ggml-hexagon.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/ggml-hexagon.cpp
index 5aa5dc1..d93e7a5 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/ggml-hexagon.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/ggml-hexagon.cpp
@@ -5193,11 +5193,18 @@ static void ggml_hexagon_precompute_matmul_params_impl(
     ggml_hexagon_precompute_hvx_mm_params(sess, src0, src1, dst, wtype, ne02, ne03, ne10, ne11, ne12, ne13, is_matmul_id, src2_row_size, vtcm_budget, kparams);
 
 finalize:
-    kparams->div_ne12_ne1 = init_fastdiv_values(ne12 * ne11);
-    kparams->div_ne1      = init_fastdiv_values(ne11);
-    kparams->div_r2       = init_fastdiv_values(ne02 > 0 ? ne12 / ne02 : 1);
-    kparams->div_r3       = init_fastdiv_values(ne03 > 0 ? ne13 / ne03 : 1);
-    kparams->div_ne11     = init_fastdiv_values(ne11);
+    {
+        // init_fastdiv_values divides by its argument. For MUL_MAT_ID ne02 is the expert count and
+        // ne12 the token count, thus one token with more than one expert gives ne12 / ne02 = 0, and
+        // an empty src1 gives ne11 = 0. A divisor of 0 becomes 1: init_fastdiv_values(1) gives the
+        // values that the arm64 division by 0 gave (it returns 0 there), thus the DSP sees no change.
+        auto div_of = [](int d) { return init_fastdiv_values(d > 0 ? (uint32_t) d : 1u); };
+        kparams->div_ne12_ne1 = div_of(ne12 * ne11);
+        kparams->div_ne1      = div_of(ne11);
+        kparams->div_r2       = div_of(ne02 > 0 ? ne12 / ne02 : 1);
+        kparams->div_r3       = div_of(ne03 > 0 ? ne13 / ne03 : 1);
+        kparams->div_ne11     = div_of(ne11);
+    }
 }
 
 static void ggml_hexagon_precompute_matmul_params(
